    <briefdescription>
<para>Explicitly load and pin a model into memory. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The model stays in memory until <ref refid="class_tryll_1_1_client_1_1_tryll_client_1a030b7da8f33425074d6539cdab625a8a" kindref="member">UnloadModel</ref> is called, regardless of whether any agents are using it.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>modelName</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Catalog model name from <computeroutput>models.json</computeroutput>. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>timeout</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Maximum time to wait; loading is slow for large GGUFs.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<parameterlist kind="exception"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>TryllError</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>If the model cannot be resolved or loaded, or on timeout. What a <ref refid="class_tryll_1_1_client_1_1_tryll_client_1a2bf3c771bceded8e342cf8e3f75a719d" kindref="member">LoadModel</ref> actually did. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
